Ladybird takes a button’s baselines from its content even where its
overflow makes it a scroll container, and the other engines do the same.
Blink’s HTMLButtonElement::AdjustStyle() sets the button’s style to
ShouldIgnoreOverflowPropertyForInlineBlockBaseline(). WebKit’s
RenderButton is a flex box, whose baselines always come from its
content. And Gecko’s ButtonControlFrame is an nsBlockFrame, which takes
its baseline from its lines. So in all three, a button sits on the line
by its text, even with “overflow: hidden”.
